# Commit when work is complete

When a coherent piece of work is finished, create the git commit(s) yourself. Do not stop at a suggested message, and do not wait for the user to ask.

- Commit in each nested repo that changed (`app/project`, `site/project`, Framework submodule, aggregator root). Leave unrelated repos untouched.
- One concern per commit. Split crash-dialog, account-book, map, and docs changes instead of bundling them.
- Subject line states why; body adds detail. No `--amend` unless the usual amend safety checks pass. Never push unless asked.
- Do not commit `public/`, `interim/`, `.playwright-cli/`, or secret files.
